The push_stream module delivers server push straight out of nginx: a
message published into a channel over HTTP reaches whoever is subscribed,
as long polling, as an EventSource stream or over a WebSocket.  The
channels live in nginx's own shared memory, so there is no broker beside
it and no backend holding a connection per subscriber.

This port only installs the module sources.  The module itself is built by
the nginx ports when their HTTP_PUSH_STREAM option is enabled.
